{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAPrdn9HTzC2ydpYxG2D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged`, which marks the receiver's current value as already seen. After calling it, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next value sent. It's the counterpart to `mark_changed` and doesn't lock the value: it just sets the receiver's version to the channel's current version (`tokio/src/sync/watch.rs:672`).\n\nI added a test, `rx_mark_unchanged`, in `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`. It covers clearing a manual `mark_changed` and clearing a change from a real `send`. The test passes with the change; without it, it doesn't compile because the method doesn't exist yet.\n\nI only ran this one test, not the full `sync_watch` suite or the loom tests. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":33819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":557,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2da33da-6cdc-4038-80d4-0701dad8c55c","uuid":"f20b096b-0aa4-405f-8b1d-7422a122f74c","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:15:01.078Z","request_id":"req_011CgAPrdY1A2ut1gZ1PSpcU"}
